<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
<meta name="description" content="Every observed 2026 NCAA FBS game, original-model replay, weekly results, market references and explicit source clocks. An auditable Sports Edge Lab research dashboard.">
<title>FBS season & market explorer · Sports Edge Lab</title>
<meta name="theme-color" content="#101b2b">
<style>
:root{color-scheme:light;--ink:#14243a;--muted:#536579;--navy:#101b2b;--line:#dbe3e8;--paper:#f5f7f8;--teal:#076b61;--teal-light:#e4f4ef;--blue:#215ecc;--amber:#905509;--amber-light:#fff3dc;--red:#a12f42;--red-light:#fbe9ed;--radius:16px}*{box-sizing:border-box}html{scroll-behavior:smooth;scroll-padding-top:20px}body{margin:0;font:16px/1.55 ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,"Segoe UI",sans-serif;color:var(--ink);background:var(--paper)}a{color:#1356ad;text-underline-offset:3px}a:hover{color:#073e82}button,input,select{font:inherit}button{cursor:pointer}button:disabled{cursor:default;opacity:.5}button,input,select,a{touch-action:manipulation}button:focus-visible,a:focus-visible,input:focus-visible,select:focus-visible,summary:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #1b77d3;outline-offset:4px}button{color:inherit}button,select,input{border:1px solid #aab9c5;border-radius:9px}button{background:white;padding:9px 14px;font-weight:650}button:hover:not(:disabled){background:#edf3f8}.skip{position:absolute;left:16px;top:-100px;padding:10px 18px;background:white;z-index:10}.skip:focus{top:10px}.topbar{background:var(--navy);color:white;border-bottom:1px solid #36445a}.topbar-inner{max-width:1440px;margin:auto;padding:19px 34px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:22px}.brand{color:white;text-decoration:none;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.015em;font-size:18px;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px}.brand-mark{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,4px);gap:4px;height:22px;align-items:end}.brand-mark i{display:block;background:#68d4bb;border-radius:2px}.brand-mark i:nth-child(1){height:10px}.brand-mark i:nth-child(2){height:17px}.brand-mark i:nth-child(3){height:22px}.nav{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:20px;font-size:14px}.nav a{color:#dbe7f2;text-decoration:none}.nav a[aria-current=page]{color:white;font-weight:750}.nav a:hover{text-decoration:underline}.hero{background:linear-gradient(115deg,#101b2b,#1c3651);color:white}.hero-inner{max-width:1440px;margin:auto;padding:40px 34px 43px}.eyebrow{text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.13em;font-size:12px;font-weight:800;color:#82d9c5;margin:0 0 10px}.hero h1{font-size:clamp(31px,4.7vw,53px);line-height:1.12;letter-spacing:-.035em;margin:0 0 17px;max-width:900px;font-weight:780}.hero-lead{color:#d9e6f0;font-size:18px;max-width:850px;margin:0}.hero-meta{margin-top:24px;display:flex;gap:14px;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center;font-size:13px;color:#d9e6f0}.hero-meta .pill{background:#25465a;color:#d0f3eb;border-color:#477667}.main{max-width:1440px;margin:auto;padding:0 34px 55px}.kpis{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:16px;margin:24px 0}.kpi{border:1px solid var(--line);background:white;border-radius:var(--radius);padding:20px 22px}.kpi-label{font-size:13px;color:var(--muted);font-weight:650}.kpi-value{font-size:36px;line-height:1.15;letter-spacing:-.035em;font-weight:780;margin:8px 0}.kpi-note{font-size:13px;color:var(--muted)}.kpi-value small{font-size:16px;font-weight:550;color:var(--muted)}.section-head{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;align-items:end;margin:31px 0 15px}.section-head h2{font-size:25px;letter-spacing:-.025em;margin:0 0 3px}.section-head p{margin:0;color:var(--muted);font-size:14px;max-width:780px}.panel{background:white;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:var(--radius);overflow:hidden}.toolbar{padding:20px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}.view-tabs{display:flex;gap:7px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:19px}.view-tabs button{border-color:transparent;border-radius:999px;font-size:14px;background:#eef2f5;padding:8px 15px}.view-tabs button[aria-pressed=true]{background:var(--navy);color:white}.view-tabs button span{font-size:12px;opacity:.85;margin-left:5px}.filter-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(190px,1.5fr) minmax(140px,.8fr) minmax(180px,1fr) minmax(190px,1.3fr);gap:14px}.filter-grid label{display:block;font-size:12px;color:var(--muted);font-weight:750;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.04em}.filter-grid input,.filter-grid select{margin-top:7px;display:block;width:100%;min-width:0;background:white;color:var(--ink);padding:11px 12px;font-size:14px;letter-spacing:normal;text-transform:none;font-weight:500}.filter-more{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;justify-content:space-between;gap:15px;align-items:center;margin-top:16px}.filter-more label{font-size:13px;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:7px}.filter-more input{width:17px;height:17px;accent-color:var(--blue)}.filter-more .hint{font-size:12px;color:var(--muted);margin:0;max-width:610px}.table-status{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:12px;align-items:center;padding:14px 20px;font-size:13px;background:#fbfcfd;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}.table-status strong{font-weight:750}.status-detail{color:var(--muted);font-size:12px}.table-wrap{overflow:auto;overscroll-behavior-inline:contain}table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;text-align:left;font-size:13px}th{font-weight:700}thead th{font-size:11px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.055em;background:#f1f5f7;color:#465b70;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);padding:13px 14px;vertical-align:bottom}tbody th,tbody td{border-bottom:1px solid #e8edf1;padding:14px;vertical-align:top}tbody tr:last-child>*{border-bottom:0}tbody tr:hover{background:#f8fbfd}.games-table{min-width:1150px}.games-table td:first-child{width:125px}.games-table th:nth-child(2){min-width:180px}.games-table td:nth-child(3){width:90px}.games-table td:nth-child(4),.games-table td:nth-child(5),.games-table td:nth-child(6){min-width:150px}.sub{display:block;color:var(--muted);font-size:11px;font-weight:450;margin-top:5px;line-height:1.45}.at{font-weight:450;color:var(--muted)}.muted{color:var(--muted);font-size:12px}.pill{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:5px;font-size:11px;font-weight:750;border:1px solid transparent;border-radius:999px;padding:3px 8px;white-space:nowrap}.pill.good{background:var(--teal-light);color:var(--teal);border-color:#bfddd3}.pill.bad{background:var(--red-light);color:var(--red);border-color:#efcdd5}.pill.quiet{background:#edf1f4;color:#52657a;border-color:#d8e1e8}.pill.warn{background:var(--amber-light);color:var(--amber);border-color:#eed9b4}.detail-button{font-size:12px;padding:6px 10px;border-color:#b7c7d3}.pagination{padding:16px 20px;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:14px;border-top:1px solid var(--line);font-size:13px}.pagination-actions{display:flex;gap:8px}.empty-state{padding:44px 24px;text-align:center;color:var(--muted)}.empty-state strong{display:block;color:var(--ink);font-size:18px;margin-bottom:7px}.explanation-strip{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:24px;margin:18px 0 25px;font-size:13px;color:var(--muted)}.explanation-strip strong{color:var(--ink)}.coverage-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:14px}.coverage-card{padding:20px;background:white;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:var(--radius)}.coverage-card h3{margin:0;font-size:16px}.coverage-card .coverage-value{margin:10px 0 3px;font-size:29px;font-weight:780;letter-spacing:-.02em}.coverage-card p{font-size:12px;color:var(--muted);margin:5px 0}.coverage-card .clock{font-size:11px;padding-top:9px;margin-top:11px;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}.coverage-card .measure{font-size:12px;color:var(--muted)}.research-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1fr;gap:18px;margin-top:18px}.text-panel{padding:23px}.text-panel h3{font-size:18px;margin:0 0 12px}.text-panel p{font-size:14px;color:var(--muted);margin:10px 0}.text-panel dl{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr auto;font-size:13px;gap:8px;margin:16px 0 0}.text-panel dt{color:var(--muted)}.text-panel dd{margin:0;font-weight:700}.footer-note{border-top:1px solid var(--line);margin-top:30px;padding-top:21px;font-size:12px;color:var(--muted)}.footer-links{display:flex;gap:18px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:13px}.check-status{display:inline-block;width:7px;height:7px;background:#71d2b6;border-radius:50%}.export{font-size:12px;padding:7px 11px}.fine{font-size:12px;color:var(--muted)}details.methods{padding:18px 22px}details.methods summary{cursor:pointer;font-weight:700;font-size:14px}details.methods p{font-size:13px;color:var(--muted);max-width:1000px}.history-table{min-width:780px}.history-table td{font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.research-callout{padding:18px 23px;background:#f3f8fa;border-top:1px solid var(--line);font-size:13px;color:#3b5367}.research-callout strong{color:var(--ink)}dialog{border:1px solid #b4c4ce;border-radius:20px;padding:0;width:min(950px,calc(100vw - 26px));max-height:calc(100vh - 30px);color:var(--ink);box-shadow:0 25px 70px #07172633}dialog::backdrop{background:#071323bb}.dialog-head{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:16px;padding:22px 25px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);align-items:start;background:#f7fafc}.dialog-head h2{font-size:24px;line-height:1.25;letter-spacing:-.025em;margin:0}.dialog-head p{margin:7px 0 0;font-size:13px;color:var(--muted)}.close-dialog{font-size:24px;line-height:1;padding:6px 10px;border:0;flex:none}.dialog-body{padding:24px}.dialog-summary{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:14px}.detail-card{border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:12px;padding:16px}.detail-card h3{font-size:13px;margin:0 0 9px;color:var(--muted)}.detail-card strong{font-size:18px}.detail-card p{font-size:12px;color:var(--muted);margin:8px 0 0}.dialog-markets{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:14px;margin-top:20px}.market-detail{border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:12px;padding:17px}.market-detail h3{margin:0 0 10px;font-size:16px}.market-detail dl{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1.2fr;gap:7px;font-size:12px;margin:0}.market-detail dt{color:var(--muted)}.market-detail dd{margin:0;word-break:break-word}.market-detail .reference{margin:9px 0;padding:9px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line);font-size:13px}.market-detail a{font-size:12px}.dialog-footer{font-size:12px;color:var(--muted);margin:20px 0 0}.chart-label{font-size:11px;fill:#566c80}.svg-chart{display:block;width:100%;height:auto}.weekly-figure{margin:0;padding:18px 22px}.weekly-figure figcaption{font-size:12px;color:var(--muted);margin-top:5px}.screenreader{position:absolute;width:1px;height:1px;padding:0;margin:-1px;overflow:hidden;clip:rect(0,0,0,0);white-space:nowrap;border:0}.noscript{padding:15px;background:var(--amber-light);color:#68450c}
@media(max-width:1000px){.filter-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}.coverage-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}.hero-inner{padding-top:32px}.kpi{padding:17px}.kpi-value{font-size:31px}}
@media(max-width:650px){.topbar-inner{padding:16px 18px;align-items:start;flex-direction:column;gap:13px}.nav{gap:18px;font-size:12px}.hero-inner{padding:29px 18px 31px}.hero-lead{font-size:15px}.hero-meta{margin-top:19px;gap:9px}.main{padding:0 14px 32px}.kpis{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:10px;margin-top:15px}.kpi{padding:15px}.kpi-value{font-size:30px}.kpi-note{font-size:11px}.section-head{margin-top:25px;align-items:start;flex-direction:column;gap:9px}.section-head h2{font-size:23px}.section-head p{font-size:13px}.toolbar{padding:15px}.view-tabs{gap:6px}.view-tabs button{font-size:12px;padding:8px 10px}.filter-grid{gap:12px}.filter-grid label{font-size:10px}.filter-grid input,.filter-grid select{font-size:12px;padding:10px 7px}.filter-more{gap:12px}.filter-more .hint{font-size:11px}.table-status{padding:12px 15px;align-items:start;flex-direction:column;gap:5px}.pagination{padding:13px 14px;font-size:12px}.pagination button{font-size:12px;padding:8px 10px}.explanation-strip,.research-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:14px}.coverage-grid{gap:10px}.coverage-card{padding:15px}.coverage-card h3{font-size:14px}.coverage-card .coverage-value{font-size:25px}.coverage-card .clock{font-size:10px}.dialog-head{padding:18px}.dialog-head h2{font-size:21px}.dialog-body{padding:16px}.dialog-summary{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:9px}.dialog-markets{grid-template-columns:1fr}.detail-card{padding:13px}.detail-card strong{font-size:16px}.weekly-figure{padding:14px}.text-panel{padding:18px}.hero h1{font-size:34px}.pagination-actions{gap:5px}}
@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){html{scroll-behavior:auto}*{transition:none!important;animation:none!important}}
</style>
</head>
<body>
<a class="skip" href="#game-explorer">Skip to all games</a>
<header class="topbar"><div class="topbar-inner"><a class="brand" href="index.html"><span class="brand-mark" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span>Sports Edge Lab</a><nav class="nav" aria-label="Main"><a href="index.html" aria-current="page">FBS season</a><a href="research.html">Historical research</a><a href="recovery.html">Recovery lab</a><a href="https://github.com/alvaromendizabal/sports-edge-lab">GitHub ↗</a></nav></div></header>
<section class="hero"><div class="hero-inner"><p class="eyebrow">NCAA FBS · 2026 season & markets</p><h1>The whole season,<br>in one view.</h1><p class="hero-lead">Every observed game stays on the board. Explore original-model replay, final scores and market references, with clear clocks and separate rolling-model records.</p><div class="hero-meta"><span class="pill"><span class="check-status" aria-hidden="true"></span>V026 recovery completed</span><span id="evidence-clock">Dated evidence · November 3, 2026</span><span>Pacific time</span></div></div></section>
<main class="main" id="main">
<section class="kpis" aria-label="Season coverage"><div class="kpi"><div class="kpi-label">Observed season games</div><div class="kpi-value" id="observed-count">888</div><div class="kpi-note" id="observed-note">622 completed · 266 scheduled</div></div><div class="kpi"><div class="kpi-label">Original replay winners</div><div class="kpi-value" id="replay-record">465 <small>/ 622</small></div><div class="kpi-note" id="replay-note">74.76% correct · retrospective</div></div><div class="kpi"><div class="kpi-label">Last calendar week</div><div class="kpi-value" id="last-record">46 <small>/ 56</small></div><div class="kpi-note">Oct 26–Nov 1 · all observed games</div></div><div class="kpi"><div class="kpi-label">This calendar week</div><div class="kpi-value" id="current-count">63</div><div class="kpi-note">Nov 2–8 · scheduled at source clock</div></div></section>
<section id="game-explorer" aria-labelledby="explorer-heading"><div class="section-head"><div><h2 id="explorer-heading">Game-by-game evidence</h2><p>Choose a view and provider. Missing market or forecast records never remove a game from the inventory.</p></div><button class="export" id="export-csv">Export comparison CSV ↓</button></div><div class="panel"><div class="toolbar"><div class="view-tabs" role="group" aria-label="Game view"><button data-view="all" aria-pressed="true">All season <span id="all-tab-count">888</span></button><button data-view="completed" aria-pressed="false">Completed <span id="completed-tab-count">622</span></button><button data-view="last" aria-pressed="false">Last week <span id="last-tab-count">56</span></button><button data-view="current" aria-pressed="false">This week <span id="current-tab-count">63</span></button></div><div class="filter-grid"><label for="game-search">Find a team or game<input id="game-search" type="search" placeholder="e.g. Ohio, Alabama, game ID" autocomplete="off"></label><label for="native-week">Season phase / week<select id="native-week"><option value="all">All native weeks</option></select></label><label for="provider-select">Market comparison<select id="provider-select"><option>DraftKings</option><option>Kalshi</option><option>Polymarket US</option><option>Polymarket Global</option></select></label><label for="horizon-select">Market observation window<select id="horizon-select"><option value="latest_pre_kickoff">Latest stored before kickoff</option><option value="T60">At or before T−60 minutes</option><option value="T120">At or before T−120 minutes</option><option value="current">Latest stored observation</option></select></label></div><div class="filter-more"><label><input id="disagreements-only" type="checkbox">Show winner disagreements only</label><p class="hint">“Latest stored” describes this archive. A recovered historical quote is useful for comparison, but it is not a forecast issued before the game.</p></div></div><div class="table-status"><div id="result-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"><strong>888 observed games</strong></div><div id="reference-status" class="status-detail">Market data and forecast eligibility are evaluated separately.</div></div><noscript><div class="noscript">JavaScript is off. All 888 observed games remain in the complete table below, with the stored DraftKings winner reference where available. Interactive filtering and detailed provider panels require JavaScript.</div></noscript><div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="All-game comparison table, horizontally scrollable"><table class="games-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Kickoff · Pacific</th><th scope="col">Game</th><th scope="col">Final score<br><span class="sub">Away · home</span></th><th scope="col">Original winner<br><span class="sub">Retrospective replay</span></th><th scope="col">Original points<br><span class="sub">Away · home</span></th><th scope="col" id="market-column">DraftKings reference</th><th scope="col">Rolling model</th><th scope="col">Evidence</th></tr></thead><tbody id="games-body">__GAME_ROWS__</tbody></table></div><div class="pagination"><span id="page-status">All 888 games · complete no-script view</span><div class="pagination-actions"><button id="previous-page" disabled>← Previous</button><button id="next-page">Next →</button></div></div></div><div class="explanation-strip"><div><strong>Original and rolling are separate.</strong> The 622 original rows are retrospective frozen-recipe replay. This snapshot has no authenticated rolling or genuinely issued new forecast. Future numeric fields stay unfilled until their inputs are verified.</div><div><strong>References are useful before they are tradable.</strong> We show captured and recovered market information with its actual clock. Trade history, candle close and de-vigged sportsbook probabilities have different meanings. All paper decisions remain NO BET.</div></div></section>
<section id="coverage" aria-labelledby="coverage-heading"><div class="section-head"><div><h2 id="coverage-heading">Provider coverage, made visible</h2><p>Every provider is checked against the same observed game inventory. Polymarket US and Global are distinct products.</p></div></div><div class="coverage-grid" id="coverage-cards"></div><div class="panel" style="margin-top:16px"><details class="methods"><summary>What each market clock means</summary><p><strong>Quote time</strong> is the timestamp represented by the source. <strong>Captured time</strong> is when that record was retrieved. A historical record recovered today can support a labelled retrospective market comparison; it cannot prove that our model possessed that information before an earlier prediction.</p><p><strong>T−120 and T−60</strong> use observations at or before the stated cutoff. <strong>Latest stored before kickoff</strong> uses a strictly earlier source timestamp. <strong>Latest stored observation</strong> may include postgame records and is clearly marked. Catalog prices with an unknown quote clock are shown only in that current-snapshot view, with the actual capture time. Candle buckets crossing a cutoff are excluded. None of these views establishes a continuously observed feed, executable fill, verified fee, profit or betting eligibility.</p><p>New market acquisition is independent of model-feature admission. Existing raw-feature validation prevents unsupported forecasts; it does not prohibit collecting schedules, history or market observations. Event matching, source rights and timestamps remain required.</p></details></div></section>
<section id="performance" aria-labelledby="performance-heading"><div class="section-head"><div><h2 id="performance-heading">Performance with its denominators</h2><p>Full-precision metrics come from authenticated owner evidence. Rounded display values do not rescore the models.</p></div><a href="research.html" class="fine">Earlier study details →</a></div><div class="research-grid"><div class="panel"><div class="text-panel"><h3>Original 622-game replay</h3><p>465 correct winners, 157 incorrect. The separate 301-game TF228 monitor has 0.465519 log loss; it does not replace this broader cohort.</p><dl id="season-metrics"><dt>Winner log loss</dt><dd>0.513328</dd><dt>Brier score</dt><dd>0.173252</dd><dt>Margin MAE / RMSE</dt><dd>14.600 / 18.185</dd><dt>Total MAE / RMSE</dt><dd>13.093 / 16.290</dd></dl></div><figure class="weekly-figure"><div id="weekly-chart"></div><figcaption>Winner correctness by native phase/week. Both wins and losses remain visible; this is replay performance.</figcaption></figure></div><div class="panel text-panel"><h3>Matched DraftKings comparison</h3><p>DraftKings performs better on the archived matched cohorts. On 192 winner games: model log loss <strong>0.604359</strong>, DraftKings <strong>0.553191</strong>. Winner disagreements: model right <strong>18</strong>, DraftKings right <strong>22</strong>.</p><dl><dt>Margin MAE · 199 matched games</dt><dd>14.325 vs 12.030</dd><dt>Total MAE · 199 matched games</dt><dd>14.637 vs 13.329</dd><dt>New rolling issues</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>Demonstrated executable edge</dt><dd>Not established</dd></dl><p>These are retrospective accuracy comparisons. New recovered provider records remain separate until exact game, product and cutoff cohorts are evaluated. No P&amp;L or ROI is invented.</p><p><a href="#game-explorer" id="view-disagreements">Inspect every winner disagreement ↑</a></p></div></div><div class="panel" style="margin-top:18px"><details class="methods"><summary>All nine weeks: winner, margin and total errors</summary><p>Authenticated inherited replay scorecards, checked against the same observed game IDs and native regular-season weeks. The calendar-week buttons above use Pacific Monday-to-Sunday boundaries; they do not rename native football weeks.</p><div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="All nine weekly model scorecards"><table class="history-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Phase / week</th><th scope="col">Games</th><th scope="col">Correct / incorrect</th><th scope="col">Log loss</th><th scope="col">Brier</th><th scope="col">Calibration ECE</th><th scope="col">Margin MAE / RMSE</th><th scope="col">Total MAE / RMSE</th></tr></thead><tbody>__WEEKLY_ROWS__</tbody></table></div></details><details class="methods"><summary>Complete replay metrics and probability calibration</summary><p>The 622-game season replay and 56-game prior calendar week use their own full-precision predictions. Calibration bins below describe the full replay; ECE is a descriptive average error, not a statistical coverage guarantee. No uncertainty interval is supplied for this replay panel.</p><div class="research-grid"><div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Complete model metrics"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Objective / metric</th><th scope="col">Season · 622</th><th scope="col">Prior week · 56</th></tr></thead><tbody>__COMPLETE_METRICS__</tbody></table></div><div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Winner calibration bins"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Probability bin</th><th scope="col">Games</th><th scope="col">Mean prediction</th><th scope="col">Home win rate</th></tr></thead><tbody>__RELIABILITY_ROWS__</tbody></table></div></div></details></div><div class="section-head"><div><h2>Historical model studies</h2><p>2024 and 2025 are exposed diagnostic seasons. Policies are selected using pre-2024 data; no current-season outcome selects or promotes a model.</p></div></div><div class="panel"><div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Historical model performance table"><table class="history-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Registered selection</th><th scope="col">Season</th><th scope="col">Games</th><th scope="col">Log loss</th><th scope="col">Brier</th><th scope="col">Accuracy</th><th scope="col">Margin MAE / RMSE</th><th scope="col">Total MAE / RMSE</th></tr></thead><tbody>__HISTORICAL_ROWS__</tbody></table></div><div class="research-callout"><strong>V026 is now an authenticated completed owner run.</strong> It completed 100 new fits and reused 197 verified states. Its mixed historical results do not authorize a new champion. The preceding V025 failure remains preserved. <a href="recovery.html">Explore the recovery mechanism →</a></div></div></section>
<footer class="footer-note"><strong>Scope:</strong> NCAA FBS-involving games only; FBS–FCS games are labelled. The observed inventory is complete within the authenticated source snapshot, but independent official-population completeness is not established. Schedule and market records are dated snapshots. No current price feed or trading service is promised.<div class="footer-links"><a href="https://collegefootballdata.com/">Schedule source: CollegeFootballData</a><a href="https://the-odds-api.com/">Sportsbook source: The Odds API</a><a href="https://docs.kalshi.com/">Kalshi API</a><a href="https://docs.polymarket.com/">Polymarket API</a><a href="https://github.com/alvaromendizabal/sports-edge-lab/tree/main/docs/fbs">Source &amp; verification</a></div><p>Public values are rounded analytical reports. Raw provider feeds, private model parameters, exact recipe configurations and cloud artifacts are excluded.</p></footer>
</main>
<dialog id="game-dialog" aria-labelledby="dialog-title"><div class="dialog-head"><div><h2 id="dialog-title">Game evidence</h2><p id="dialog-subtitle"></p></div><button class="close-dialog" id="close-dialog" aria-label="Close game details">×</button></div><div class="dialog-body"><div class="dialog-summary" id="dialog-summary"></div><div class="dialog-markets" id="dialog-markets"></div><p class="dialog-footer" id="dialog-footer"></p></div></dialog>
